  "summary": "The Menlo Park City Council voted 3-1 on Oct. 8, 2024 to authorize an agreement with Flock Safety to install 35 fixed automated license plate readers for at least two years, at first-year cost of $133,000. Residents from Sharon Heights urged expansion citing burglaries, while dissenting council member Betsy Nash and one resident raised privacy and Fourth Amendment concerns.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "In a 3-1 vote Tuesday night, Oct. 8, the City Council authorized executing an agreement for Flock to provide and operate 35 fixed ALPR cameras in Menlo Park for at least two years.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "We still have not seen data that ALPRs reduce residential burglaries or crime in general",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    },
    {
      "quote": "Because Flock data records place and time, movement may be deduced, which constitutes a search, which then requires a warrant",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    }
  ],
